data: {"research_task_id": "387a5090b27550c59de86adb415eb26e", "event_seq": 19, "type": "worker", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T15:58:02Z", "payload": {"content_hash": "fca92358a25a3418b48b418da3d16a5a170136fefcafc47495b432a98cd19093", "node_key": "tool:387a5090b27550c59de86adb415eb26e:s3:search_paper_catalog:a4107ba84e89", "node_type": "tool", "parent_node_key": "agent:387a5090b27550c59de86adb415eb26e:s3", "parent_source_event_id": "research-event:387a5090b27550c59de86adb415eb26e:16", "result_id": "search_paper_catalog", "result_length": 9759, "status": "completed", "summary": "检索完成：来源=USENIX Security（全局目录），命中 5 篇候选论文。\n1. Dos and Don'ts of Machine Learning in Computer Security\n   catalog_paper_id: bf973b6a0943cb3d3165ec26e72e6915\n   candidate: {\"title\":\"Dos and Don'ts of Machine Learning in Computer Security\",\"catalog_paper_id\":\"bf973b6a0943cb3d3165ec26e72e6915\",\"conference_id\":\"usenix-security\",\"year\":2022,\"source_page_url\":\"[已隐藏链接]\",\"source_links\":[\"[已隐藏链接]\"]}\n   详情页: [已隐藏链接]\n   摘要: With the growing processing power of computing systems and the increasing availability of massive datasets, machine learning algorithms have led to major breakthroughs in many different areas. This development has influenced computer security, spawning a series of work on learning-based security systems, such as for malware detection, vulnerability discovery, and binary code analysis. Despite great potential, machine learning in security is prone to subtle pitfalls that undermine its performance and render learning-based systems potentially unsuitable for security tasks and prac", "tool_name": "search_paper_catalog"}}

